<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">11042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Zero tankers crossed the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> on Wednesday, and only six passed on Thursday despite the ceasefire — Iranian mines still litter the waterway and shipping firms won't risk US sanctions to clear them.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Saudi Arabia's bypass pipeline has lost ten percent capacity, destroying the market's main workaround.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Even if talks succeed, relief at the pump is months away... and the ceasefire hasn't stopped the bleeding.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran's parliament speaker set two preconditions before negotiations with Washington can begin — a Lebanon ceasefire and the release of frozen assets — while the US wants nuclear concessions Tehran has already ruled out.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Pakistan, hosting the talks in Islamabad, cut diesel prices by a hundred and thirty-five rupees per litre on the same day, the largest single fuel reduction in the country's history, linking it directly to the ceasefire it brokered.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Whether Islamabad can bridge positions this far apart will define its most ambitious diplomatic gamble.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel struck the Nabatieh government complex in southern Lebanon and killed thirteen state security officers — not Hezbollah fighters, but civil servants at a government building.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>It's the largest single death toll for Lebanese officials since the war began.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The two sides are set to meet at the US State Department on Tuesday, though it's hard to see how Lebanon negotiates after burying its own.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Eighty US service members sought conscientious objector discharge in March alone — nearly double the usual annual total.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Hotline calls have risen a thousand percent since the war began, with many citing the bombing of a girls' school in Minab as their breaking point.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The last time the American military saw dissent at this pace was Vietnam, and that was a conscript army — this one is volunteer.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Trump told Fox News he'd armed Kurdish groups to open a second front against Iran from inside Iraq — and every Kurdish party denied receiving weapons.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>All six factions and the White House now give directly opposing accounts of the alliance.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>It's a rare case of a proxy strategy collapsing because the proxies publicly refused the role.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sudan's General Burhan named hardliner al-Atta as chief of staff on the same day healthcare workers in Nyala went on strike and the army launched a new offensive on Kurmuk.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The reshuffle signals the military prefers escalation over any negotiated settlement.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Civilians are losing medical access in a warzone while their generals prepare for more fighting.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Egypt extended Ahmed Douma's detention by fifteen more days — the man it pardoned in twenty twenty-three after a decade in prison, then re-arrested for writing about his own imprisonment.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>A judge will now decide whether to free someone Cairo has summoned seven times since his release.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The pattern is its own message: pardon, silence, re-arrest.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Twenty-two apartheid-era detainees were killed in South African custody, and not a single person has been prosecuted.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>State prosecutors deliberately sabotaged Truth and Reconciliation Commission cases to protect apartheid-era killers, according to testimony before the Khampepe Commission on Thursday.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Whether prosecutors can themselves face criminal charges for that sabotage is now the question before the court.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>European airports have given Brussels a three-week deadline — forty percent of the continent's jet fuel flows through Hormuz, and prices have more than doubled to over eighteen hundred dollars per tonne.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Even reopening the strait leaves two to three months of supply lag before fuel reaches European tanks.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Airlines face grounding decisions before that deadline expires.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>HSBC won Hong Kong's first stablecoin licence, placing digital currency infrastructure in the hands of banks rather than crypto startups.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The monetary authority issued two licences — to HSBC and a Standard Chartered venture — while the US Congress has debated stablecoin rules for three years without acting.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Banks across Asia and Europe are watching whether Hong Kong's framework becomes the global template.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India produces twenty percent of the world's generic antibiotics, and pharmaceutical effluent from production cities is seeding antibiotic resistance genes into urban water systems.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Resistance spreads from factory runoff to rivers to hospital wards, where once-treatable infections are becoming lethal.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The pipeline from production to resistance is now documented — what's missing is any plan to interrupt it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A study of eight hundred cyclones since nineteen eighty-one found that storm damage nearly doubles when seas are abnormally warm.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Marine heatwaves are intensifying faster than coastal risk models are being updated.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The gap between what's coming and what governments are planning for widens with every hurricane season.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>University of Barcelona researchers used drone imaging and AI to identify climate-resilient wheat varieties in a single growing season — work that traditionally takes years of field trials.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Wheat faces accelerating climate stress worldwide, and the varieties that'll survive the next decade need to be identified now.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Global breeding programs are watching whether this method scales beyond the lab.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Scientists at Shark Bay in Australia observed stromatolite microbes interacting with complex cells in real time — the exchange theorized to have sparked eukaryotic life two billion years ago.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Until now, that process existed only as a hypothesis, never directly witnessed.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Researchers can now test which environmental triggers drive the transition from simple to complex life, God willing opening a new chapter in biology.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>North Korean operatives posed as a quant-trading firm at a cryptocurrency conference, spent six months building access inside exchange Drift, then stole two hundred and eighty million dollars.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The funds moved through shell companies using the same pipeline Pyongyang built to evade US and UN sanctions.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>It's the clearest demonstration yet that North Korea's cyber program isn't espionage — it's a revenue stream.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>France is migrating its government systems from Windows to Linux, treating Microsoft the way it once treated Russian gas — as a strategic dependency to unwind.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The shift accelerated as EU-US tensions over the Iran war deepened, with Paris framing digital sovereignty as national security.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Other European governments are watching whether a nation can exit Microsoft at scale, or whether the dependency runs too deep to break.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>